{
 "thread": "R883wP8ukpo",
 "subject": "Regarding the LPA models with different parameterization",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2019-06-13T11:59:45Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "SY7CskvIAgAJ",
   "from": "Dangubic, M. (Marija)",
   "author": "3fc1965ba2ce931e",
   "date": "2019-06-13T11:47:40Z",
   "subject": "Regarding the LPA models with different parameterization",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"NL\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Dear TidyLPA Team, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am a PhD Candidate at Utrecht University and I am analyzing my data using the latent profile analysis. Since it is the first time I am using this analysis, I explored my data using both tidyLPA and mclust packages\r\n in R and I have some questions for you. If you have time, I would really appreciate your answer.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<ol style=\"margin-top:0cm\" start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Do you maybe know of a good source to better understand models with different parameterization?\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Mclust offers 14 different  models and the tidyLPA offers six of them. What is the reason to choose only those six?\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Since the authors of mclust talk in terms of shape, volume and orientation and the terms used in tidyLPA are variances and covariances, can someone explain how these terms compare?<u></u><u></u></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-US\">I think running the same models in Mplus would help my understanding. Do you maybe have codes to run all these mclust models in Mplus? I am new to Mplus and I am not sure how to use\r\n it to run the same models that mclust offers. <u></u><u></u></span></li></ol>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thank you very much in advance. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Kind regards, </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Marija Dangubic</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "UFY0o_TIAgAJ",
   "from": "Rosenberg, Joshua",
   "author": "f235054bd9ff417a",
   "date": "2019-06-13T11:59:45Z",
   "subject": "Re: Regarding the LPA models with different parameterization",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hi Marija, thank you for your message. See my responses below (though I welcome others to add to them):</div>\r\n<div lang=\"NL\">\r\n<div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">Do you maybe know of a good source to better understand models with different parameterization?\r\n</span></li></ol>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">This was a real challenge for me, initially - but think we figured out a way to communicate them effectively. We tried to document the six parameterizations in terms of their covariance\r\n matrix as well as verbal descriptions of them here: <a href=\"https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html#model-specification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html%23model-specification&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3D5Dj7Kp4jH6p22bh6xGdK\">https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html#model-specification</a></span></font></div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\" style=\"border-spacing:0px\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:wf_segoe-ui_light,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html#model-specification\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:var(--themePrimary)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html%23model-specification&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3D5Dj7Kp4jH6p22bh6xGdK\">tidyLPA - data-edu.github.io</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\nLatent Profile Analysis (LPA) is a statistical modeling approach for estimating distinct profiles, or groups, of variables. In the social sciences and in educational research, these profiles could represent, for example, how different youth experience dimensions\r\n of being engaged (i.e., cognitively, behaviorally, and affectively) at the same time.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://data-edu.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://data-edu.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Vle5sHQUXJNxYZsp8fc5K\">data-edu.github.io</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">Mclust offers 14 different  models and the tidyLPA offers six of them. What is the reason to choose only those six?\r\n</span></li></ol>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">These are the six most common parameterizations. Indeed, for LPA, often, only one (what in tidyLPA is the first model type - Equal variances, and covariances fixed to 0.</span></font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">Since the authors of mclust talk in terms of shape, volume and orientation and the terms used in tidyLPA are variances and covariances, can someone explain how these terms compare?</span></li></ol>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">See the link above.</span></font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">I think running the same models in Mplus would help my understanding. Do you maybe have codes to run all these mclust models in Mplus? I am new to Mplus and I am not sure how to use it to run the same models that mclust offers.\r\n</span></li></ol>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div lang=\"NL\"><div><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">You can simply change the package argument (for estimate_profiles), as follows, to run them in MPlus:</span></font></div>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">\r\n<pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:13px;display:block;padding:9.5px;margin:0px 0px 10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border:1px solid rgb(238,238,238);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-radius:0px;overflow:auto\">m &lt;- pisaUSA15[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">:</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">100</span>, ] <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">%&gt;%</span>\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">    </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102)\"><a href=\"https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/single_imputation.html\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(55,95,132)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/single_imputation.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2TvZH-UBQYPAiP9baioBXb\">single_imputation</a></span>() <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">%&gt;%</span>\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">    </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102)\"><a href=\"https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/estimate_profiles.html\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(55,95,132)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/estimate_profiles.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OTXN1245oHYO4Tl2ZWA0h\">estimate_profiles</a></span>(2, package = &quot;MplusAutomation&quot;) <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\"> </span>\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">    </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102)\"><a href=\"https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/compare_solutions.html\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(55,95,132)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://data-edu.github.io/tidyLPA/reference/compare_solutions.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2CtET2EW23kWw56eCowU7c\">compare_solutions</a></span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">statistics =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102)\"><a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/base/topics/c\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(55,95,132)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/base/topics/c&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zQsqjjQLQSv-ueuwtU9nC\">c</a></span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;AIC&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;BIC&quot;</span>))</code></pre>\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">It may need some processing, but, the Mplus model code would then be saved to the `m` object; you can access it via:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\">\r\n<div lang=\"NL\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><span style=\"color:rgb(32,31,30);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,0);display:inline!important\">m$model_1_class_2$model$input</span></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<div lang=\"NL\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<br>\r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;tidyLPA&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tidylpa+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0U6bzMJKrHuCvw8-IZcmVp\">https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/AM0PR05MB4401095DFCC92D73AE85738784EF0%40AM0PR05MB4401.eurprd05.prod.outlook.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/AM0PR05MB4401095DFCC92D73AE85738784EF0%2540AM0PR05MB4401.eurprd05.prod.outlook.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OFjf8cUk7X9FpXRBzkQoe\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/AM0PR05MB4401095DFCC92D73AE85738784EF0%40AM0PR05MB4401.eurprd05.prod.outlook.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496038419000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0uh-ehu8gKJz0J31n-1tdD\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
